@PACKAGE_INIT@

# Deliberately no find_dependency() calls. Every dependency is PRIVATE behind
# $<BUILD_INTERFACE:>, so none appears in INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES and none has
# to be resolvable by a consumer (#41 §10).
#
# This is the payoff for not shipping the archive. A static nodehammer would
# leave every private dependency undefined until the consumer's final link, so
# this file would have to find_dependency() the lot — ten packages a consumer has
# no reason to know about. If that variant is ever added, this file grows the
# branch.
#
# Note this covers *linking*, and how a dependency is satisfied differs by kind.
# The static ones (zstd, flatbuffers, manifold, miniz, …) are absorbed into the
# library and disappear. A shared backend — ROOT or DD4hep, when those importers
# are enabled — stays a DT_NEEDED reference instead, and nothing here records
# where it lives: no INSTALL_RPATH is set, deliberately, because baking absolute
# paths in would not survive an LCG view being swapped underneath it. Such a
# build therefore expects its backends on the loader path, which is what sourcing
# the view already does. Set CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH_USE_LINK_PATH at configure time
# if you want a self-contained install instead.

include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/nodehammer-targets.cmake")

check_required_components(nodehammer)
